From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 03 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: pcd: dump the raw FE management-index free-list in fe_buffer

T-M6-8 VLAN-freeze dig. The retired inline-FE-VM-opcode VLAN path
freezes at exactly 5+tnums=21 packets, and every session that
investigated it (decomp/fe-action-interpreter.md) read only the two
params-page pointer/counter fields fe_buffer already exposes
(+0x54 = internalFEBufferManagementIndexAddr, +0x58 =
internalFEBufferDepletionCounter) -- nobody ever dumped what +0x54
actually points AT.

Recovered the real vendor layout from the NXP SDK source in this repo
(kernel/patches or, canonically, ASK/patches/kernel/
010-ask-fman-dpaa-ehash.patch, FmPortSetFESupport, ~L9117):
FM_MURAM_AllocMem(pcd, 5 + totalNumOfTnums, 4) is not a bare counter,
it is a byte-array free-list:

  byte 0          cursor (initialized to 4)
  bytes 1..3      low bytes of the FE internal buffer pool's own
                  MURAM offset (packed into the same 32-bit word
                  whose top byte becomes the cursor)
  bytes 4..4+n-1  free-list of tnum indices 0..tnums-1
  byte 4+n        0xFF terminator

fman_pcd_fe_buffer_show() already loops every armed port and prints
+0x54/+0x58; this patch adds one more line per port, reading and
hex-dumping the full (5+tnums)-byte array +0x54 points at (skipped
when +0x54 is 0, i.e. FE support not armed on that port). Read-only,
debugfs-gated (root), same ioread8()/fman_muram_offset_to_vbase()
pattern already used elsewhere in this file (see the cc_test key-dump
code a few hundred lines below).

Purpose: correlate the free-list's live cursor/contents between a
sustaining routed flow and a freezing VLAN flow (once the retired F-233
inline-opcode path is rebuilt on the fevm-vlan-investigation branch)
to see directly whether entries are handed out but never pushed back,
rather than continuing to infer it from IC-level microcode reads.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: A (read-only debugfs
addition to an existing root-only node; no new state, no write path,
no behavior change when FE support is unarmed)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
index 6bfa0976..70abbbb8 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -3940,6 +3940,7 @@ static int fman_pcd_fe_buffer_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 	for (port_id = 0x08; port_id <= 0x11; port_id++) {
 		struct fman_port *port = fman_port_lookup_rx(pcd->fman, port_id);
 		u32 pp_off;
+		u8 tnums;
 		if (!port)
 			continue;
 		pp_off = fman_port_get_params_page(port);
@@ -3948,8 +3949,35 @@ static int fman_pcd_fe_buffer_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 		pp = (void *)(void *)fman_muram_offset_to_vbase(muram, pp_off);
 		v54 = ioread32be((void __iomem *)((u8 __iomem *)pp + 0x54));
 		v58 = ioread32be((void __iomem *)((u8 __iomem *)pp + 0x58));
+		tnums = fman_port_get_total_tnums(port);
 		seq_printf(s, "port 0x%02x: +0x54=%#010x +0x58=%#010x tnums=%u\n",
-			   port_id, v54, v58, fman_port_get_total_tnums(port));
+			   port_id, v54, v58, tnums);
+
+		/*
+		 * T-M6-8 VLAN-freeze dig: dump the raw (5+tnums)-byte
+		 * management-index array v54 points at (FmPortSetFESupport,
+		 * SDK 999-patch ~L14545 / F-072): byte 0 = cursor, bytes
+		 * 1-3 = low bytes of the FE internal buffer pool's MURAM
+		 * offset, bytes 4..4+tnums-1 = the free-list of tnum
+		 * indices (0..tnums-1), byte 4+tnums = 0xFF terminator.
+		 * Nobody has read this array's live contents before - every
+		 * prior probe only read the +0x54/+0x58 pointer/counter
+		 * pair, never what the pointer actually points at. v54 is
+		 * only valid once FE support has been armed on this port.
+		 */
+		if (v54) {
+			void __iomem *idx = (void *)(void *)
+				fman_muram_offset_to_vbase(muram, v54);
+			int n = 5 + tnums;
+			int i;
+
+			seq_printf(s, "  idx[%#06x] cursor=%u:",
+				   v54, ioread8(idx));
+			for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
+				seq_printf(s, " %02x", ioread8(
+					(void __iomem *)((u8 __iomem *)idx + i)));
+			seq_puts(s, "\n");
+		}
 	}
 	return 0;
 }
